[3692]="70027226\n1\tComplete Tadhrien's woodworking task\tTadhrien is in the Crafting Hall in Esteldín. You should speak with Tadhrien about your advancement in woodworking.\n2\tTalk to Tadhrien in Esteldín\tTadhrien in the Crafting Hall in Esteldín. You should speak with Tadhrien to continue your advancement in crafting.\n",
[3693]="700072FC\n1\tTalk to Gwaloth\tGwaloth is on a terrace overlooking Celondim, located south of the top of the stairs that wind up the hillside around which the city is constructed. The Elf Mibrethil suggested that you speak with his friend Gwaloth if you are interested in learning a crafting trade.\n",
[3694]="70025B64\n1\tExecute the recipe for hard tack rations\030Execute the recipe for strawberry pie-filling\030Execute the recipe for beef stew\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the three recipes required by Jewel Underhill for your growth as a Cook. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n2\tDeliver the hard tack rations to Odo Pipes\030Bring the strawberry pie-filling to Ned Diggins\030Deliver the beef stew to Carlo Blagrove\tHobbits in need of the food you cooked can be found throughout Michel Delving. You should bring your cooked goods to the hobbits in Michel Delving. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n3\tReturn to Jewel Underhill with news of your success\tJewel Underhill can be found in the Crafting Area of Michel Delving. You should return to Jewel Underhill with the news that your cooked foods were greatly appreciated by the local hobbits.\n",
[3695]="700271E8\n1\tExecute the recipe for hard tack rations\030Execute the recipe for strawberry pie-filling\030Execute the recipe for beef stew\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the three recipes required by Jewel Underhill for your growth as a Cook. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n2\tDeliver the hard tack rations to Odo Pipes\030Bring the strawberry pie-filling to Ned Diggins\030Deliver the beef stew to Carlo Blagrove\tHobbits in need of the food you cooked can be found throughout Michel Delving. You should bring your cooked goods to the hobbits in Michel Delving. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n3\tReturn to Jewel Underhill with news of your success\tJewel Underhill can be found in the Crafting Area of Michel Delving. You should return to Jewel Underhill with the news that your cooked foods were greatly appreciated by the local hobbits.\n",
[3696]="70025BFD\n1\tExecute the recipe for a green onion crop\030Execute the recipe for sweet galenas pipe-weed\030Execute the recipe for a cabbage crop\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the three recipes required by Olo Proudfoot for your growth as a farmer.\n2\tBring the green onion crop to Hereward Loamsdown in The Ivy Bush\030Bring the sweet galenas pipe-weed to Opal Goodbody\030Bring the cabbage to Bogo Chubb\tHobbits in need of the crops you grew can be found throughout Hobbiton. You should bring your crops to the hobbits in Hobbiton.\n3\tReturn to Olo Proudfoot, the expert farmhand in Hobbiton\tOlo Proudfoot, the expert farmhand, can be found in the farmlands of Hobbiton. You should return to Olo Proudfoot with the knowledge that your crops were a great success with the townsfolk.\n",
[3697]="70025C36\n1\tExecute the recipe for a polished ruby\030Execute the recipe for a gold ring\030Execute the recipe for a gold bracelet\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the three recipes required by Daemirdan for your growth as a jeweller. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n2\tDeliver the polished ruby to Eón\030Deliver the gold ring to Celephadh\030Deliver the gold bracelet to Nethúr\tThe people who wish to receive the pieces of jewellery you made can be found throughout Esteldín. You should deliver your jewellery-pieces to the folk of Esteldín. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n3\tReturn to Daemirdan with news of your success\tDaemirdan can be found in the Esteldín Craft Hall. You should return to Daemirdan with news of your success.\n",
[3698]="7002721D\n1\tExecute the recipe for a polished ruby\030Execute the recipe for a gold ring\030Execute the recipe for a gold bracelet\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the three recipes required by Daemirdan for your growth as a jeweller. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n2\tDeliver the polished ruby to Eón\030Deliver the gold ring to Celephadh\030Deliver the gold bracelet to Nethúr\tThe people who wish to receive the pieces of jewellery you made can be found throughout Esteldín. You should deliver your jewellery-pieces to the folk of Esteldín. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n3\tReturn to Daemirdan with news of your success\tDaemirdan can be found in the Esteldín Craft Hall. You should return to Daemirdan with news of your success.\n",
[3699]="70025C99\n1\tExecute the recipe for a steel helm\030Execute the recipe for steel gloves\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the two recipes required by Molda for your growth as a Metalsmith.\n2\tBring the steel helm to Egil Oldbeard\030Bring the steel gloves to Tandri Greyhammer\tDwarves who wish to receive the pieces of armour you forged can be found throughout Thorin's Hall. You should deliver your crafted items to the dwarves of Thorin's Hall.\n3\tReturn to Molda in the Maker's Hall\tMolda is in the Maker's Hall, the crafting area in Thorin's Hall. You should return to Molda with news of your success.\n",
[3700]="70027221\n1\tExecute the recipe for a steel helm\030Execute the recipe for steel gloves\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the two recipes required by Molda for your growth as a Metalsmith.\n2\tBring the steel helm to Egil Oldbeard\030Bring the steel gloves to Tandri Greyhammer\tDwarves who wish to receive the pieces of armour you forged can be found throughout Thorin's Hall. You should deliver your crafted items to the dwarves of Thorin's Hall.\n3\tReturn to Molda in the Forging Hall\tMolda is in the Forging Hall, the crafting area in Thorin's Hall. You should return to Molda with news of your success.\n",
[3701]="70025C9A\n1\tExecute the recipe for a scroll of scholar-lore\030Execute the recipe for a scroll of battle-lore\030Execute the recipe for a scroll of warding-lore\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the three recipes required by Forgamthan for your growth as a Scholar. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n2\tBring the scroll of scholar-lore to Mirwen\030Bring the scroll of battle-lore to Lindir\030Bring the scroll of warding-lore to Faimir\tElves who are interested in your scrolls can be found throughout Rivendell. You should bring the scrolls you crafted to various Elves in Rivendell. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n3\tReturn to Forgamthan with news of your success\tForgamthan can be found in Elrond's Library in Rivendell. You should return to Forgamthan with the news that your scrolls were greatly admired by the Elves who took them.\n",
[3702]="70027223\n1\tExecute the recipe for a scroll of scholar-lore\030Execute the recipe for a scroll of battle-lore\030Execute the recipe for a scroll of warding-lore\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the three recipes required by Forgamthan for your growth as a Scholar. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n2\tBring the scroll of scholar-lore to Mirwen\030Bring the scroll of battle-lore to Lindir\030Bring the scroll of warding-lore to Faimir\tElves who are interested in your scrolls can be found throughout Rivendell. You should bring the scrolls you crafted to various Elves in Rivendell. WARNING: All items required for this quest must be kept intact, and should not be consumed in the completion of a larger recipe. If you use one of your required Quest Items as an ingredient, you will not be able to complete the quest until you make a new one!\n3\tReturn to Forgamthan with news of your success\tForgamthan can be found in Elrond's Library in Rivendell. You should return to Forgamthan with the news that your scrolls were greatly admired by the Elves who took them.\n",
[3703]="70025C3F\n1\tExecute the recipe for a cotton cloak\030Execute the recipe for sturdy leather armour\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the two recipes required by Fladdan for your growth as a Tailor.\n2\tBring the cotton cloak to Eón\030Bring the sturdy leather armour to Herondan\tPeople in need of the tailored items you have sewn can be found throughout Esteldín. You should bring your sewn goods to the townsfolk of Esteldín.\n3\tTalk to Fladdan in the Esteldín Crafting Hall\tFladdan can be found in the Crafting Hall in Esteldín. You should speak with Fladdan and tell him of the successful deliveries of the goods you made.\n",
[3704]="7002721E\n1\tExecute the recipe for a cotton cloak\030Execute the recipe for sturdy leather armour\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the two recipes required by Fladdan for your growth as a Tailor.\n2\tBring the cotton cloak to Eón\030Bring the sturdy leather armour to Herondan\tPeople in need of the tailored items you have sewn can be found throughout Esteldín. You should bring your sewn goods to the townsfolk of Esteldín.\n3\tTalk to Fladdan in the Esteldín Crafting Hall\tFladdan can be found in the Crafting Hall in Esteldín. You should speak with Fladdan and tell him of the successful deliveries of the goods you made.\n",
[3705]="70025CB8\n1\tExecute the recipe for the bright steel greatsword\030Execute the recipe for a bright steel dagger\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the two recipes required by Thithrandi for your growth as a weaponsmith.\n2\tBring the bright steel greatsword to Hagan\030Bring the bright steel dagger to Albryc Longfoot\tDwarves who wish to receive the goods you made can be found throughout Thorin's Hall. You should bring the weapons and components you forged to the interested dwarves in Thorin's Hall.\n3\tReturn to Thithrandi in the Maker's Hall\tThithrandi can be found in the Maker's Hall in Thorin's Hall. You should return to Thithrandi with the news that your weaponsmithy abilities were admired by the dwarves of Thorin's Hall.\n",
[3706]="70027225\n1\tExecute the recipe for the bright steel greatsword\030Execute the recipe for a bright steel dagger\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the two recipes required by Thithrandi for your growth as a weaponsmith.\n2\tBring the bright steel greatsword to Hagan\030Bring the bright steel dagger to Albryc Longfoot\tDwarves who wish to receive the goods you made can be found throughout Thorin's Hall. You should bring the weapons and components you forged to the interested dwarves in Thorin's Hall.\n3\tReturn to Thithrandi in the Forging Hall\tThithrandi can be found in the Forging Hall in Thorin's Hall. You should return to Thithrandi with the news that your weaponsmithy abilities were admired by the dwarves of Thorin's Hall.\n",
[3707]="70025CB9\n1\tExecute the recipe for a yew spear\030Execute the recipe for a yew bow\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the two recipes required by Tadhrien for your growth as a woodworker.\n2\tDeliver the yew spear to Rhona\030Deliver the yew bow to Eón\tYour goods can be delivered to various people around Esteldín. Many folks around Esteldín have taken an interest in your woodworking skills.\n3\tTalk to Tadhrien in Esteldín\tTadhrien is in the Crafting Hall in Esteldín. You should speak with Tadhrien and tell her of your successful deliveries.\n",
[3708]="70027227\n1\tExecute the recipe for a yew spear\030Execute the recipe for a yew bow\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel. You should craft the two recipes required by Tadhrien for your growth as a woodworker.\n2\tDeliver the yew spear to Rhona\030Deliver the yew bow to Eón\tYour goods can be delivered to various people around Esteldín. Many folks around Esteldín have taken an interest in your woodworking skills.\n3\tTalk to Tadhrien in Esteldín\tTadhrien is in the Crafting Hall in Esteldín. You should speak with Tadhrien and tell her of your successful deliveries.\n",
[3709]="70007A47\n1\tBring a glittering copper ring to Barton Tyne\030Collect glittering copper ring\tBarton Tyne is on the road between the town of Bree and The Forsaken Inn. Barton Tyne has told you that he lost his wedding ring, and he is looking for the services of a jeweller to make a glittering copper ring to replace it. His wife Verity is sure to be furious if he returns without it.\n",
[3710]="700077E5\n1\tBring bronze armour and a bronze buckler to Osur Stouthammer\030Collect bronze buckler\030Collect bronze armour\tOsur Stouthammer is in the crafting hall near the Boar Fountain in the town of Bree. Osur Stouthammer is concerned by the low quality of the armour worn by the guards of the town of Bree and wants you to find a metalsmith willing to make some bronze armour and a bronze buckler he can give to the defenders.\n",
[3711]="70007437\n1\tBring two rowan camp-fire kits to Crocus Stonybanks\030Collect rowan camp-fire kits (total: 2)\tCrocus Stonybanks is in Overhill. Crocus has asked you to bring her two rowan camp-fire kits so she can go camping with her friends.\n",
[3712]="700072FE\n1\tBring polished agates to Guleneth\030Collect polished agate (total: 3)\tGuleneth is at Celondim in Ered Luin. Jeweller Guleneth has asked you to acquire three polished agates that he can use to complete some of the pieces he has left unfinished.\n",
